    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46759" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠθ-έω</span></b> , aor. 1
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤθησα </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤθισα</span> codd.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				gloss on 
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦσα</span>
			, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤθω</span>
			:—
				Med.
			, aor. 1
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠθησάμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Al.</u>
					324
				</span></i>
			: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤθω</span>): <i>-sift, strain</i>, Nic.l.c.:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be strained</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἠθούμενον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Cra.</u>
					402d
				</span></i>
			; [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶνος] ἠθημένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epil.
					6
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρυσὸς ἠθημένος διὰ πέτρας</span>
			<i>filtered through</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				59b
			</span></i>: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ τετρημένης [τὴν
				ῥῆσιν] ἠθεῖ</span>
			<i>lets it trickle out</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Herod.
				3.33
			</span></i>.</div>
